.el .ds Aq '
.TH pgloupe-logs 1  "logs " 
.SH NAME
pgloupe\-logs \- Work with Postgres server logs
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpgloupe logs\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Work with Postgres server logs
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
pgloupe\-logs\-dump(1)
Decode a log (csvlog, jsonlog or stderr; compression is detected) and print each record as JSON
.TP
pgloupe\-logs\-analyze(1)
Summarize one or more logs: statements with percentiles, errors, locks, temp files, connections, checkpoints and autovacuum
.TP
pgloupe\-logs\-ingest(1)
Add logs to a store; files already ingested are skipped and grown ones replace their old version
.TP
pgloupe\-logs\-report(1)
Report on a time window of a store
.TP
pgloupe\-logs\-fetch(1)
Download a time range of log files from a managed service or server (resumable)
.TP
pgloupe\-logs\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
